WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.741 --> 00:00:16.112
That winter was especially cold and wet.

2
00:00:17.513 --> 00:00:23.199
There was snow, sleet, or rain almost every day for weeks, and the wind made things even worse.

3
00:00:25.281 --> 00:00:28.564
It was miserable standing at the cab stand for hours at a time.

4
00:00:30.172 --> 00:00:33.433
At least Captain and I only had to put up with it for half a day each.

5
00:00:34.773 --> 00:00:39.014
Poor Jerry was out there all day, huddled in his cab trying to keep warm.

6
00:00:41.375 --> 00:00:45.696
To help him through it, Polly often sent Dolly to the cab stand with hot food.

7
00:00:47.017 --> 00:00:53.398
One such cold, rainy day, Jerry had barely started eating when a gentleman came hurrying toward us, raising

8
00:00:53.458 --> 00:00:56.139
his umbrella to signal that he wanted to hire the cab.

9
00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:03.315
When Jerry saw him, he immediately handed his bowl back to Dolly, who was still standing there keeping

10
00:01:03.355 --> 00:01:03.895
him company.

11
00:01:05.256 --> 00:01:06.037
"No, no!"

12
00:01:06.677 --> 00:01:09.039
the gentleman cried when he saw what Jerry was doing.

13
00:01:09.059 --> 00:01:11.541
"Finish your soup, my friend.

14
00:01:12.662 --> 00:01:17.445
I don't have much time to spare, but I can wait until you're done and your little girl

15
00:01:17.545 --> 00:01:19.026
is safely off toward home."

16
00:01:20.868 --> 00:01:23.950
With that, he climbed into the cab and sat down to wait.

17
00:01:24.690 --> 00:01:26.832
Jerry thanked him, and then turned to Dolly.

18
00:01:27.624 --> 00:01:30.725
"That's a true gentleman, Dolly," he told her quietly.

19
00:01:31.826 --> 00:01:36.008
"He isn't too wrapped up in his own concerns to spare a thought for a poor cabman and

20
00:01:36.048 --> 00:01:36.488
his girl!"

21
00:01:37.908 --> 00:01:40.449
He quickly finished his soup, and sent Dolly home.

22
00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:47.812
We drove the gentleman to his destination, and I suppose he was pleased with our work because after

23
00:01:47.852 --> 00:01:49.873
that he hired us on a regular basis.

24
00:01:50.974 --> 00:01:52.334
The gentleman's name was Mr.

25
00:01:52.354 --> 00:01:58.694
Wright. I think he was fond of horses, because he often stopped to pat me and give me

26
00:01:58.734 --> 00:01:59.415
a kind word.

27
00:02:00.496 --> 00:02:04.239
It's a rare thing indeed for customers to pay any attention to a cab horse.

28
00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:09.704
With few exceptions, most people would be just as likely to pat the engine of a train!

29
00:02:11.326 --> 00:02:12.006
One day Mr.

30
00:02:12.026 --> 00:02:15.830
Wright and a gentleman friend of his hired our cab to take them to do some shopping.

31
00:02:18.272 --> 00:02:20.534
The second gentleman went into a store while Mr.

32
00:02:20.574 --> 00:02:22.056
Wright stood and waited outside.

33
00:02:23.848 --> 00:02:24.529
I saw Mr.

34
00:02:24.589 --> 00:02:29.012
Wright watching a pair of fine-looking horses that were standing across the street in front of a wine

35
00:02:29.052 --> 00:02:29.712
seller's cart.

36
00:02:31.353 --> 00:02:35.696
Their driver was nowhere in sight, and after a few minutes the horses grew restless.

37
00:02:36.937 --> 00:02:39.479
They weren't tied, so they started forward on their own.

38
00:02:40.439 --> 00:02:44.202
They'd only gone a few steps down the street when a man emerged from the nearest shop.

39
00:02:45.383 --> 00:02:47.484
He raced after the cart, shouting angrily.

40
00:02:48.545 --> 00:02:52.688
When he caught up to the horses, he immediately started whipping both of them as hard as he

41
00:02:52.728 --> 00:02:56.349
could. He even struck them on their heads.

42
00:02:56.729 --> 00:02:57.970
It was terrible to watch!

43
00:02:59.651 --> 00:03:00.831
Mr. Wright saw it all.

44
00:03:01.852 --> 00:03:04.293
He crossed the street and hurried toward the wine cart.

45
00:03:06.274 --> 00:03:07.415
"Stop that right now!"

46
00:03:07.875 --> 00:03:09.856
he called to the driver in a stern voice.

47
00:03:09.876 --> 00:03:15.319
"Otherwise I'll have you arrested for leaving your horses unattended and for cruel conduct!"

48
00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:18.361
The man spun around, looking surprised.

49
00:03:19.502 --> 00:03:21.002
He frowned and cursed at Mr.

50
00:03:21.063 --> 00:03:23.404
Wright, but at least he stopped whipping the horses.

51
00:03:25.068 --> 00:03:27.369
As the driver jumped into his cart, Mr.

52
00:03:27.409 --> 00:03:30.971
Wright pulled out a notebook and wrote down the name and address painted on the cart.

53
00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:32.851
"What are you doing?"

54
00:03:33.151 --> 00:03:34.192
the driver demanded.

55
00:03:35.352 --> 00:03:35.813
But Mr.

56
00:03:35.853 --> 00:03:37.713
Wright merely smiled and didn't answer.

57
00:03:38.634 --> 00:03:41.515
He returned to the cab just as his friend came out of the shop.

58
00:03:43.035 --> 00:03:45.716
When the friend heard what had been going on, he laughed.

59
00:03:46.117 --> 00:03:52.379
"Don't you have enough business of your own to look after, Wright, without worrying about other people's horses

60
00:03:52.419 --> 00:03:53.139
and servants?"

61
00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:54.100
he said.

62
00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:57.342
Mr. Wright frowned and was silent for a moment.

63
00:03:57.362 --> 00:04:01.124
"Do you know why this world is as bad as it is?"

64
00:04:01.524 --> 00:04:03.346
he said at last in a serious tone.

65
00:04:03.366 --> 00:04:06.148
"No," his friend said.

66
00:04:06.168 --> 00:04:11.591
"Why?" "It's because people think only about themselves," Mr.

67
00:04:11.631 --> 00:04:12.252
Wright told him.

68
00:04:12.272 --> 00:04:16.415
"They aren't willing to help the oppressed or stand up to wrongdoers.

69
00:04:18.116 --> 00:04:22.099
I can't watch anyone acting in a cruel way without trying to put a stop to it.

70
00:04:23.319 --> 00:04:27.485
If I didn't, I'd consider myself just as guilty as the one committing the wrong."

71
00:04:28.586 --> 00:04:32.668
"I see your point, my friend," the other gentleman said, sounding impressed.

72
00:04:33.788 --> 00:04:34.648
Mr. Wright nodded.

73
00:04:34.668 --> 00:04:40.351
"Many a business owner has thanked me for letting him know his horses were being mistreated.

74
00:04:41.491 --> 00:04:43.572
I'm sure the wine seller will be no exception.

75
00:04:44.332 --> 00:04:46.653
Let's go right now and let him know what I saw."

76
00:04:47.974 --> 00:04:50.375
Jerry had been sitting in the cab listening to all this.

77
00:04:51.415 --> 00:04:52.576
He tipped his cap to Mr.

78
00:04:52.616 --> 00:04:57.371
Wright. "I wish there were more gentlemen like you, sir," he said.

79
00:04:57.391 --> 00:04:59.418
"The city would be better for it."
